# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Roster environment configuration
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database — ANY PostgreSQL with the pgvector extension available.
# The database is fully provider-agnostic: point these at local Docker,
# a self-hosted Postgres on EC2, Supabase, Neon, RDS, etc.
#
# The local Docker default (see docker/docker-compose.yml). Host port is 5433
# to avoid clashing with any Postgres already running locally on 5432.
#
# Deploying on Vercel + Supabase (see README.md's "Deploying" section): use
# Supabase's POOLED connection string here (Transaction pooler, port 6543,
# with ?pgbouncer=true appended) — Vercel's serverless functions each open
# their own connection, and an unpooled Postgres runs out fast.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://roster:roster@localhost:5434/roster?schema=public"

# Direct (non-pooled) connection used for migrations. For serverless/pooled
# targets (Neon, Supabase pooler, PgBouncer) set this to the direct URL.
# For local Docker it is identical to DATABASE_URL.
#
# On Supabase: the direct connection string (port 5432, no pooler) — some
# migration operations aren't compatible with PgBouncer's transaction mode.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://roster:roster@localhost:5434/roster?schema=public"

# development | test | production
NODE_ENV="development"

# ── Auth.js ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session secret used to sign/encrypt the JWT. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 33
AUTH_SECRET=""

# Optional: canonical app URL. Auth.js infers it in dev; set in production
# (e.g. https://roster.example.com).
# AUTH_URL=""

# ── Google OAuth ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Client (type: Web application) in the Google Cloud
# console. Authorized redirect URI (local dev):
#   http://localhost:3005/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# ── BYOK vault ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side secret used to encrypt stored provider keys (AES-256-GCM).
# Must decode to exactly 32 bytes. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# ── Rate limiting (optional) ─────────────────────────────────
# Shared, cross-instance rate limiting via Upstash's REST Redis. Falls back
# to an in-memory, per-process limiter when unset (fine for local dev/single
# instance).
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""

# ── Sentry (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Error tracking, client + server + edge. A DSN isn't secret (it only allows
# *sending* events), so one NEXT_PUBLIC_ var covers every runtime. Sentry.init
# no-ops safely when unset — errors just aren't reported anywhere.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""
#
# CI-only, for uploading source maps on deploy (never needed for local dev —
# the Sentry Next.js build plugin reads these itself and silently skips
# upload when they're absent):
# SENTRY_ORG=""
# SENTRY_PROJECT=""
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=""

# ── Eval harness (optional, CLI only) ────────────────────────
# Configure any subset of the three tiers, then run `npm run eval`.
# Only *_API_KEY is required — PROVIDER/MODEL default to Anthropic
# (claude-opus-5 / claude-sonnet-5 / claude-haiku-4-5, see
# src/config/model-tiers.ts) with built-in per-token pricing, so avg cost is
# reported automatically with zero extra config.
#   EVAL_<TIER>_PROVIDER  catalog id: openai | anthropic | google | groq | custom | … (default: anthropic)
#   EVAL_<TIER>_MODEL     model id (default: per-tier Anthropic model)
#   EVAL_<TIER>_API_KEY   provider API key (required to activate this tier)
#   EVAL_<TIER>_BASE_URL  optional (custom / openai-compatible endpoints)
#   EVAL_<TIER>_INPUT_PRICE_PER_MTOK / EVAL_<TIER>_OUTPUT_PRICE_PER_MTOK
#                         optional, USD per 1M tokens. Only needed if you
#                         override PROVIDER/MODEL away from the default —
#                         otherwise that tier just won't report a cost
#                         (never a guessed one).
EVAL_FRONTIER_API_KEY=""
EVAL_MID_API_KEY=""
EVAL_CHEAP_API_KEY=""
#
# Optional: for agents with a knowledge base (Phase 7), configure an
# embedding-capable provider (openai | google only) so grounded eval tasks
# actually retrieve. Requires the agent's KB to already be ingested with this
# SAME provider (`npm run ingest`) — ingestion and query embedding must match.
# Without this, grounded tasks (graders with type "retrieval") run ungrounded
# and fail their recall check.
# EVAL_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER="openai"
# EVAL_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=""
# EVAL_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=""
